 "notes": "Black-hole superradiance bound from spins of heavy jetted AGNs (Unal, Pacucci & Loeb). Curve is the lower envelope in f_a of the union of all excluded regions in Figure 6 (mu vs f_axion plane, scalar/axion case), extracted from the vector PDF axiondecayconstantvsmass.pdf in the e-print; both the 'measured' (Table 2, light purple) and 'calculated/SMFP-predicted' (Table 3, rainbow) AGN regions are included, as the paper presents their combination as its result. Excluded region: f_a ABOVE the envelope (weak self-interaction), i.e. 1/f_a below the reported curve is excluded. Reported as 1/f_a in GeV^-1 (canonical). Mass range 2.95e-21 to 1.72e-17 eV matches the text's quoted scalar exclusion 2.9e-21 - 1.7e-17 eV. Spin lower bounds are at 2-sigma confidence per Sec. 2.2. Superradiance bound does not assume a local DM density.",
